  "concept": "Prodromal PD: RBD, hyposmia and risk prediction",
  "slug": "prodromal-pd-rbd-hyposmia-and-risk-prediction",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:048b017e497e744d3c81e089452283edf6f7b083e204c30cae7fa0cd212d930f",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "a965123fbaa442ae951398d9c24f2845d65cea52a876f79db85bf2c3ed01cb5c",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:6384747cd0ac274689b2f7d136979b41c3bb64629a4ef5abca1d559b124ba117",
      "text": "A 2024 Mayo Clinic retrospective study matched 186 women and 186 men with iRBD; 48 patients (12.9%) phenoconverted during median follow-up of 6.0 years. Only age at diagnosis remained associated with conversion in the adjusted model (HR 1.09, 95% CI 1.06\u20131.13); the unadjusted association with antidepressant use must not be interpreted as evidence of neuroprotection. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515114/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0ed75a8e46b225d9ce59c0546d3d66965fffc77b18c3c17c1b064afe69ede6c3",
        "ev:67307a490cdd04ef41bcabf6e901ec59916ba710af5a290613a010daa83dd8a6",
        "ev:83b45988209982943c477f25bd2a1cd02a3cff8dd5e70888929b26ac5bd5ce2b",
        "ev:8f7928ce2d9987670b3a957b8f861879d99b176f56687a7cf5a10080aa493529",
        "ev:a85ae2a90ecc43f0ca0b913f62bbad0a26447ed1c275c6bfda8f30f9b6d51594",
        "ev:d31d4d87d98d7c3fe235ad0a6b084e331ad9813e3a43843f042f2d03c8f3967f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a7f2bd7fc49ced63d5f7de225f91061932de3c1b49673e9cd236b0d3f7d76ce4",
      "text": "Isolated RBD involves dream enactment and loss of normal REM sleep atonia in the absence of an established neurodegenerative disorder. The cited risk cohorts used polysomnography-confirmed RBD; their estimates should not be assigned to questionnaire-positive dream enactment alone. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515114/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11208573/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3367cd32c55721bf6f070c5bc85301b5b0d666b9d61f4b3c43657d2d58186063",
        "ev:a85ae2a90ecc43f0ca0b913f62bbad0a26447ed1c275c6bfda8f30f9b6d51594",
        "ev:c23d8b815596baac1696e00a97c896e78e7cb12ea37b1145de284e0ff02d4f91",
        "ev:f7c6805f56302d06cffdea3a511e90a904376513bddbea4f4e0b3fd3c9d736c7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9a68b45e011f4759fc11c0f541dc434c2e4936f6808df995d3ec71a413c59af4",
      "text": "Isolated RBD is a strong prodromal marker for a spectrum of neurodegenerative outcomes, including Parkinson\u2019s disease, dementia with Lewy bodies and multiple system atrophy; a reported overall phenoconversion rate is therefore not a PD-only conversion rate. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515114/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:623d50578d71b9ce132aaa3c8ceaaaeb5073dffb12a14f244c81ed0c404e78e2",
        "ev:c1d7022d70afd00da8a94963961540bbe996c16ad51424b12d11de10c2257979"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:522968c29e113121b725d847d14ea66af102c9f8511f817ced81cf9da8e6d04f",
      "text": "A 2019 meta-analysis of seven prospective studies reported an association between hyposmia and subsequent PD, with pooled relative risk 3.84 (95% CI 2.12\u20136.95) across follow-up periods of 3\u201317 years. This relative risk is not an absolute probability that a person with hyposmia will develop PD. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6545790/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1385b4442dc1e2cec42bde03a974c6827a0f91407b5d5afc21a46cecc708f2b5",
        "ev:b096353a93be1a771fc2e0a628d83bfccc5bc0bed051353d882e3051bfcab0b0",
        "ev:cb986d23f5be9d810a9b04c94dbf67ce0fa7351d99b29f7d3e72df5b6c6f30e2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:36720800010cc578519ca966018a4ddbd93e907c7357244491efe539c4a6c84a",
      "text": "RBD conversion estimates depend on population, age, endpoint definitions and ascertainment. The 2019 multicentre investigators warned that predictor hazard ratios should not be extrapolated to the general population, and the 2024 Mayo investigators called for population-based, polysomnography-confirmed cohorts to quantify community risk. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515114/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:19fd9226c305f5a4b503f7d298a5b6124e109e3decc762fee3080ec526ae7af7",
        "ev:2ed79a85fc68c8482b2d209093e8d63da547e22c4297501f118f98a41f8ce62d",
        "ev:5c9ab7cd719df9d4340ccece0e9e2fe675db945b1a1a29fbc5a9f0ad47616219",
        "ev:8328db83c18000e215b8918b6abe53108dea02f03125dda759de1b37c35ebbc8",
        "ev:bf482586c04e8a6789c566ce861e0496d99982423eb1b2d081acc0564c843322",
        "ev:d31d4d87d98d7c3fe235ad0a6b084e331ad9813e3a43843f042f2d03c8f3967f",
        "ev:d88a727f9bd16bc62d973e6990b3ee9ac90f1be2161a696062c4845c805e27f4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:266178ee2aa2158b3f64602e86981f6dd3719a1264bdfc5d80697d27361886e4",
      "text": "A negative baseline prodromal assessment cannot reliably rule out later phenoconversion in iRBD. In the 2019 cohort, even participants negative for the MDS prodromal criteria had conversion estimates of 5% at 3 years, 13% at 5 years and 27% at 8 years. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2d95b9ab60fffd0b6382581b5c215c03ac67b1d62d48de78fd1a3626e2a5f625",
        "ev:2ed79a85fc68c8482b2d209093e8d63da547e22c4297501f118f98a41f8ce62d",
        "ev:35335bb7f5cbc699cc32298ad09851be106e5d707449777b7cf178cd5b15ea51",
        "ev:704153ddd1e0512eb3bc25768a9a8d7a0bd95f0545b5ad3331c97f70da40fc1b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:acd6da48a2301217ea8a7dedd8dc0cf195eb4a3986abae8d01ce40b417fc9536",
      "text": "The MDS research framework combines an age-based prior probability with marker likelihood ratios in a Bayesian na\u00efve classifier; probable prodromal PD means at least 80% estimated certainty that prodromal disease is present, rather than an 80% prediction of clinical conversion within a specified number of years. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26474317/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11208573/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:49825057e5532c34b1fcf7c2129bdf8f824493bb77f7952a73339762713c3420",
        "ev:4d37bd478049f494aa685a049703fdaaf099e085422deed2a5ce85a45667ed01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:729fb45ad1cb839c031ff365ca30cf4a5edbee3b00f308b1453ef76040c11d9a",
      "text": "Postuma and colleagues\u2019 2019 study followed 1280 polysomnography-confirmed iRBD patients from 24 centres: mean age was 66.3 years, 82.5% were men, and mean follow-up was 4.6 years. Overall conversion to an overt neurodegenerative syndrome was 6.3% per year, with Kaplan\u2013Meier estimated conversion of 73.5% at 12 years; these are study estimates rather than universal individual prognoses. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9be358a076c62ff5e05e65e770ff6eba9af7a1c3a31e9d019293e11361b98993",
        "ev:d88a727f9bd16bc62d973e6990b3ee9ac90f1be2161a696062c4845c805e27f4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:856de9915f6d0d75220764a70b8d390c168566753d94395752a405d7483e1e1b",
      "text": "The 2024 Lifelines analysis found poor discrimination (ROC-AUC 0.577) using a subset of MDS risk and prodromal markers in 160 self-reported PD converters and 320 matched controls. Only six of eleven risk markers and six of twelve prodromal markers could be inferred, so this result scopes a partial, largely questionnaire-based implementation rather than invalidating the complete criteria. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11208573/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:62fddc0b0c1e31c5b1f919a5260572a31020f272119d797405d1dd871aedad9b",
        "ev:d3c3e47510b470bfca22f6e6289f00d2171f48b4a69fddd19bead57fbc8352d0",
        "ev:e1d49e3ff8bc9645a33efa11aaa968e67761b6d5faad5b6fd5e7fef16bcc7353",
        "ev:fc5a2af279b3ba70861fada0c83ac75ba5f139d15e25831f0f71c963fea21c5f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:2bcf971804976ea14dc6872ca8ca3899cdc8939769f6e493698056fe137e4656",
      "text": "Prodromal PD describes early symptoms or signs of neurodegeneration before fully evolved motor parkinsonism permits a classic clinical diagnosis; the original MDS prodromal criteria were explicitly developed for research purposes only. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26474317/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:d66419683ae1fa0c0e95585545d5bb07c797c68c3b54651a2e7a4508a8472be0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5c2bfb79951523b445c729d0cdeaf75266d8e7b9987817b3c8707aa64d6c3543",
      "text": "In the same 2019 iRBD cohort, olfactory deficit predicted faster phenoconversion (adjusted hazard ratio 2.62), alongside quantitative motor abnormalities (3.16) and mild cognitive impairment (1.91\u20132.37); the outcome was overall neurodegenerative phenoconversion. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2ed79a85fc68c8482b2d209093e8d63da547e22c4297501f118f98a41f8ce62d",
        "ev:8a41d205c8607a86de523f4793dd4aa300b6018d0e93342eaaf40a20b6cb0a78"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:06937ba6de7f9705851ec586c5e0167d96ba91eb4e599621a08e7a89bcf90dc4",
      "text": "Smell loss alone has limited specificity: it can occur in neurological diseases other than PD. The hyposmia meta-analysis explicitly cautioned that the limited evidence did not establish hyposmia as a solid stand-alone predictor of PD. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6545790/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:852f543d4d49c2f99a2f3e51f2ef7405f9612d3467de01d8aa344aeccae0686a",
        "ev:da68f2eba426023599e21c36508f84e02dbbff35f29c4192cb5b58f5cadee923"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:48ec133998f223e67ac52c0589e27c7f54fbd70d61de6d45dfb7b01caaee5415",
      "text": "The 2019 update of the MDS prodromal framework revised marker weights using new prospective evidence; in particular, the positive likelihood ratio for olfactory loss increased, while many marker likelihood ratios were unchanged. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31412427/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:25b86da61a934bb1385c7027b3fad3ec63a5cef7ef2f40c3c82171284674753d",
        "ev:c981a20aad428cfcb5ad784b91d4b4431440e5c3d9b30763bac522d31c6fe20a"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
    {
      "assertionId": "prose:5432fe84f256d0e7f88dd3f79f30dcf0723487969729100bda3338c47ce3a6f5",
      "statementSha256": "5432fe84f256d0e7f88dd3f79f30dcf0723487969729100bda3338c47ce3a6f5",
      "assertionKind": "summary",
      "index": 0,
      "documentSlug": "prodromal-pd-rbd-hyposmia-and-risk-prediction",
      "documentConcept": "Prodromal PD: RBD, hyposmia and risk prediction",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:048b017e497e744d3c81e089452283edf6f7b083e204c30cae7fa0cd212d930f",
      "text": "Prodromal PD research estimates disease probability before classic motor diagnosis by combining age and risk-marker information. Polysomnography-confirmed isolated REM sleep behaviour disorder is a strong marker, but its phenoconversion outcomes include dementia and other disorders as well as PD. Hyposmia is associated with increased subsequent PD risk yet has limited specificity. Cohort conversion percentages, relative risks and Bayesian prodromal probabilities describe different quantities and should not be substituted for an individual forecast. The MDS research framework and its 2019 update support research stratification; the 2019 multicentre RBD study, 2024 Mayo cohort and 2024 Lifelines analysis demonstrate why population, ascertainment, marker availability and follow-up matter.",
      "sources": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11208573/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11515114/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6391615/",
